      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sherburn incorporated as a village on March 8, 1879, marking its formal establishment in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://lakesnwoods.com/Sherburn.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Steam locomotives stopped every 15 miles, a factor that helped place Sherburn’s railroad station where it stands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherburn%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the mid‑1860s, George Archer ran a sod tavern on Lake Manyaska’s north bank, just south of Sherburn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherburn%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sherburn’s post office has been in continuous operation since 1879, serving the community for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
